  "verdict_tag": "NOT FIXABLE -- (b) complex-route Yee-ization fails; go to (ii). Stuck on: C1_Nprop(emergent-local route inert, stays 4); C4_locality(N_prop=2 op non-local, R29/R35-barred); C5_emergence(Yee-ization = R30 hand-built, not emergent walk)",
  "verdict": "The (b) half CANNOT be fixed by an emergent-walk Yee-ization. MECHANISM (numbers decide): the R30 KINEMATIC identity IS present on the reassembled complex (|inc . exact-gauge| = 1.1e-16, machine zero), so R30's curl annihilates EXACT placed-gauge curvature. But the emergent walk's +w gauge-dominant modes ALREADY carry zero gauge-sector curvature (|inc . gauge-part(S_curv)| = 7.2e-16); their propagating curvature lives ENTIRELY in a small NON-GAUGE admixture (|inc . nongauge-part| >= 1.06). So applying the R30 gauge-curl is INERT: N_prop stays [4], never 2 (bit-for-bit svn unchanged) -- the complex route has nothing to bite on the gauge sector. The ONLY operation that reaches N_prop=2 is projecting the +w modes onto ker C (deleting the 5-18% non-gauge admixture) -- and that projector is NON-LOCAL (direction-dependence 2.01 at k->0, the SAME R29/R35 pathology as P_S=2.449 / slave=1.215). Equivalently, the only LOCAL unitary that installs exact ker-C modes is R30's hand-built product-of-local-shears leapfrog -- an EXISTENCE construction, NOT the QCA-emergent walk. TWO criteria that do NOT block: C3 TT is bit-invariant (residual 3.1e-16) and C2 the J5 co-cone HOLDS for the R30 leapfrog target (|w_leapfrog - w_walkshell| <= 3.3e-16 across theta in [0.4, 1.047, 1.0, 1.2]). So (b) is stuck JOINTLY on STRICT LOCALITY (the N_prop=2 operation is non-local) and EMERGENT MATTER (the local alternative is hand-built R30, not emergence) -- NOT on J5, NOT on TT, NOT on exact constraint per se. SIGNAL not theorem: (ii) adjudication draws the conclusion. This was the LAST fixable hypothesis (PI order); deliver (ii).",
